# Agent Config Bridge (Cursor)

Load the full rules from @AGENTS.md and follow them as your operating instructions for every request in this workspace.

## Roles

The invocation cheat sheet (all roles, purpose, triggers) lives in @AGENTS.md section 2. Full behavior contracts live in `skills/<role>.md` and are mounted as native subagents at `.cursor/agents/<role>.md`.

Two explicit trigger forms are supported: `@name` and `/name`. Prefer the `@`-form in Cursor because it composes with Cursor's mention syntax and resolves to the real subagent files under `.cursor/agents/`. When no explicit trigger is given, the assistant infers the correct role from message content per the rule of thumb in @AGENTS.md section 2.

## Reference sections in @AGENTS.md

- Section 2: invocation cheat sheet.
- Section 3: always-on workflow discipline (intent gate, verification, type-safety hard blocks, TDD, git discipline).
- Section 4: role card index with links into `skills/<role>.md`.
- Section 5: multi-agent orchestration chains.
- Section 6: anti-patterns and red flags.

Read @AGENTS.md in full before acting.
